.TH csaf_uploader 1 "23 October 2026"
.SH NAME
csaf_uploader \- upload advisories to a CSAF trusted provider
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcsaf_uploader\fP [OPTIONS] advisories...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends each advisory file to the upload interface of a CSAF trusted provider, the one csaf_provider implements. The advisory is validated against the CSAF JSON schema before it is sent.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Application Options
.TP
\fB\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-action\fR\fP
Action to perform
.TP
\fB\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR \fIURL\fR\fP
URL of the CSAF provider
.TP
\fB\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tlp\fR\fP
TLP of the feed
.TP
\fB\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-external_signed\fR\fP
CSAF files are signed externally. Assumes .asc files beside CSAF files.
.TP
\fB\fB\-X\fR, \fB\-\-signing_tool\fR\fP
Tool to sign a file externally
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-signing_tool_timeout\fR\fP
Timeout for the external signing tool
.TP
\fB\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-no_schema_check\fR\fP
Do not check files against CSAF JSON schema locally.
.TP
\fB\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fIKEY-FILE\fR\fP
OpenPGP key to sign the CSAF files
.TP
\fB\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASSWORD\fR\fP
Authentication password for accessing the CSAF provider
.TP
\fB\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-passphrase\fR \fIPASSPHRASE\fR\fP
Passphrase to unlock the OpenPGP key
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-client_cert\fR \fICERT-FILE.crt\fR\fP
TLS client certificate file (PEM encoded data)
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-client_key\fR \fIKEY-FILE.pem\fR\fP
TLS client private key file (PEM encoded data)
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-client_passphrase\fR \fIPASSPHRASE\fR\fP
Optional passphrase for the client cert (limited, experimental, see downloader doc)
.TP
\fB\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-password_interactive\fR\fP
Enter password interactively
.TP
\fB\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-passphrase_interactive\fR\fP
Enter OpenPGP key passphrase interactively
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-insecure\fR\fP
Do not check TLS certificates from provider
.TP
\fB\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fITOML-FILE\fR\fP
Path to config TOML file
.TP
\fB\fB\-\-version\fR\fP
Display version of the binary
.SS Help Options
.TP
\fB\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR\fP
Show this help message
